            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0228" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/2082: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-09T16:00:00-05:00">March 9, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. For Myron Taylor. Reference Embassy’s telegram 135, February 28, 8 p.m. and
                    London Embassy’s no. 408, February 17, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p>You may inform Winterton that this Government is prepared to accept an invitation
                    to attend a full meeting of the Intergovernmental Committee at some time in the
                    spring. As to the place of the meeting we prefer a neutral to a belligerent
                    capital or would accept Monte Carlo.</p>
                <p>Repeat to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
